- `messages[:\s].{0,40}exceeds limit` hmm, variants: `messages: array length 2051 exceeds limit 2048` covered by the first. "too many messages" — add. "messages count exceeds" — add.

But these patterns go into `_overflowPatterns` (making isContextOverflow true) — good. And a separate parse function extracts M.

**Coalesce step**: merge adjacent tool-call/result pairs into compact messages. Simplest correct implementation: iterate the message list; group runs of (AssistantMessage with toolCalls followed by their ToolResultMessages) and replace each group older than the newest user message with a single user text message: `[coalesced N tool turns: <tool names> — results elided]`. Keep system prompt? The system prompt in this codebase is separate (`Context.systemPrompt`). "never drops the newest user message or the system prompt" — system prompt is separate field; but coalesce works on messages list. Keep all user messages except... hmm "only whole tool-call/result pairs older than the cut point go" — the cut point is the newest user message.

