Target count: coalesce until under cap − margin, or everything droppable is coalesced. Merging pairs one group at a time reduces count by (groupSize - 1) per group. Group of assistant+result = 2 → 1. If cap is 2048 and count is 2059, coalescing alone can't realistically get under... each merge saves 1 message. Coalescing 11 groups saves 11. Hmm, that's not a "real reducer" — the ticket acknowledges: coalesce first (fast), then compaction pass (the real reducer). So the reactive repair: coalesce the outbound payload (helps marginally + makes room), then run a compaction pass over the live transcript via host relief hook (that reduces the transcript durably), rebuild context, retry once.

