Simpler formulation that guarantees pairing safety: find a "cut" — everything before cut index C is "old region", where C ≤ newestUserIndex and the old region boundary lands such that no tool group straddles it (i.e., C is at a group boundary). Within the old region, group messages into: tool-groups (assistant w/ calls + its results) → each becomes one carrier user message; consecutive plain messages (user text / assistant text) merge into one carrier. Then while still over target and more old region remains, merge carriers together.

Implementation approach (deterministic):
1. Compute group boundaries in the old region: a group = tool-call group (assistant with toolCalls + subsequent ToolResultMessages until all answered) or a single other message.
2. Convert each group to a carrier `UserMessage.text('[coalesced N message(s): tool calls a, b → results elided]')`.
3. Result count = messages.length - (sum of (groupSize - 1)).
4. If still > target: merge adjacent carriers pairwise (or all into one).

