}
```

ModelCapsStore implements it. `learnedCapFor` consults pins first then learned; `learnFromRefusal` records (only upgrades: unknown→cap, cap→different cap re-learn E4; never downgrade to unknown? If refusal isUnknown and we already have a cap, keep the cap — a differently-shaped error shouldn't unlearn).

For dart:io usage — check if lib uses dart:io anywhere (e.g. memory store?). Let me check quickly for an existing pattern of persisted JSON store in lib outside cli. There's `lib/src/memory/` probably with file persistence. I'll check.

Also `coalesceMessagesForCap`:

```dart
List<Message> coalesceMessagesForCap(List<Message> messages, {required int targetMessageCount}) {
 if (messages.length <= targetMessageCount) return messages;
 // Cut point: the newest user message is never coalesced away — pairing-
 // safe groups older than the newest user message merge into single
 // user-text carrier messages.
 var newestUserIndex = -1;
 for (var i = messages.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
   if (messages[i] is UserMessage) { newestUserIndex = i; break; }
 }
 ...
}
```

Coalescing algorithm:
- Build output list. Region = indices `[0, newestUserIndex)`. Walk region: accumulate "groups":
 - a group starts at an AssistantMessage with toolCalls; consumes following ToolResultMessages answering those calls; also absorbs adjacent text-only assistant/user messages? The ticket: "merge adjacent tool-call/result pairs and old turns into compact messages". 
 - I'll merge: runs of consecutive messages that are (assistant-with-toolCalls + their results) OR text-only assistant messages OR user messages (other than the newest) into one user text message per run. Actually simpler and safer: iterate; when the current output count is over target, merge maximal runs of non-newest-user messages into carriers. But we must preserve pairing: only remove WHOLE call/result groups. Text-only assistant messages and non-newest user messages are safe to merge too.

Simpler formulation that guarantees pairing safety: find a "cut" — everything before cut index C is "old region", where C ≤ newestUserIndex and the old region boundary lands such that no tool group straddles it (i.e., C is at a group boundary). Within the old region, group messages into: tool-groups (assistant w/ calls + its results) → each becomes one carrier user message; consecutive plain messages (user text / assistant text) merge into one carrier. Then while still over target and more old region remains, merge carriers together.

Implementation approach (deterministic):
1. Compute group boundaries in the old region: a group = tool-call group (assistant with toolCalls + subsequent ToolResultMessages until all answered) or a single other message.
2. Convert each group to a carrier `UserMessage.text('[coalesced N message(s): tool calls a, b → results elided]')`.
3. Result count = messages.length - (sum of (groupSize - 1)).
4. If still > target: merge adjacent carriers pairwise (or all into one).

If newestUserIndex == -1 (no user message)? Then everything is droppable in theory, but "never drops the newest user message" — no user message exists; keep the last message regardless: treat cut as messages.length - 1 (keep last message untouched). Edge E3/E2.

Also run `repairToolPairing` on the result? The carriers are user messages; the kept region was untouched; the boundary between old region and kept region: old region ended at a group boundary,…

