### Files to create/modify:

**A. `lib/src/overflow.dart`** — add message-cap patterns + `MessageCapRefusal` + `classifyMessageCapError`.

```dart
final class MessageCapRefusal {
 const MessageCapRefusal({this.maxMessages});
 final int? maxMessages;
 bool get isUnknown => maxMessages == null;
}

MessageCapRefusal? classifyMessageCapError(String? errorMessage) {
 if (errorMessage == null || errorMessage.isEmpty) return null;
 if (_nonOverflowPatterns.any((p) => p.hasMatch(errorMessage))) return null;
 final m = _messageCapLimitPattern.firstMatch(errorMessage);
 if (m != null) {
   final limit = int.tryParse(m.group(2)!.replaceAll(',', ''));
   if (limit != null) return MessageCapRefusal(maxMessages: limit);
   return const MessageCapRefusal(); // cap-unknown (E1)
 }
 if (_messageCapShapePatterns.any((p) => p.hasMatch(errorMessage))) {
   return const MessageCapRefusal(); // cap-unknown
 }
 return null;
}
```

Message-cap shape patterns (also added to `_overflowPatterns` so isContextOverflow is true):
- `RegExp(r'array length \d+ exceeds limit \d+', caseSensitive: false)` — incident shape
- `RegExp(r'\bmessages?\b[^.]{0,60}\bexceeds? (?:the )?limit\b', ...)` hmm careful. Ticket variants: `messages: array length 2051 exceeds limit 2048` (covered by first), `array length N exceeds limit M` generic (covered), `too many messages`, `messages count exceeds`.
- `RegExp(r'\btoo many messages\b', caseSensitive: false)`
- `RegExp(r'\bmessages count exceeds\b', caseSensitive: false)`

And the limit-parse pattern: `RegExp(r'array length (\d[\d,]*) exceeds limit (\d[\d,]*)', caseSensitive: false)`.

