- First the cap heal (before pairing heal):

```dart
     // gh-1680 self-healing retry: a provider message-cap 400 means the
     // outbound ARRAY (not the tokens) exceeded the model's per-request
     // cap. Learn the cap from the error, coalesce the next payload, run
     // ONE host compaction pass, retry ONCE — a wedged session recovers
     // here instead of re-failing every heartbeat. A second refusal
     // surfaces normally (no infinite loop).
     if (_needsCapHeal(capHealed, finished, config)) {
       capHealed = true;
       final refusal = classifyMessageCapError(finished.errorMessage)!;
       config.messageCapPolicy!.learnFromRefusal(config.model, refusal);
       final learned = config.messageCapPolicy!.learnedCapFor(config.model);
       capCoalesceTarget = learned == null
           ? null
